  "id": "routing/a-room-opened-for-no-one-keeps-its-first-sender",
  "title": "A room the host opened naming no one under the recipient key, the key absent, null, empty or blank, is its first sender's: a second sender gets a room of his own, and the first is found again and answered twice",
  "rules": [
    "§10.4",
    "§5.7",
    "§10.1 step 2"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: tests/test_shared_channel_routing.py::TestARoomTheHostOpened::test_a_room_opened_for_no_one_keeps_its_first_sender, one channel per case. Once two rooms are bound to the number, the first sender is found by her binding.",
